","title":"Demo update. Your Next Fest feedback addressed!","summary":"Thanks to everyone playing Street Value during Next Fest. You gave us some fantastic feedback and even discovered a bug or two. Well this update addresses them. FixesRepaying the Shark now clears the whole debt. The amount box was rounding to the nearest $100, which left some of you owing him $44 forever. Sorry about that.Tooltips are now on a solid panel with wrapped text, and they scale with the Large Text setting.The side column now tells you what's below the fold (\"More below: Empire · Conne","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-20T21:40:04Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706696827","verified_at":"2026-10-21T00:38:39Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5335560-1846651706691553","game_id":"steam-5335560","kind":"announcement","title":"The Street Value demo is live for Next Fest!","summary":"The demo is live!!! Street Value is my solo project: the old Drugwars trading game rebuilt as a roguelite deckbuilder. The free demo is up for all of Steam Next Fest (Oct 19 to 26), and it covers the first 10 days of a run. So what is Street Value?You owe a loan shark in 90s New York and you've got 30 days to pay him back. Every card does one of two jobs: Hustle cards work the market. Buy in bulk, hype a price, sell before the block crashes.Street cards get you out when a cop turns the corner.Th","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-19T17:05:17Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706691553","verified_at":"2026-10-21T00:38:39Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"}],"analyses":[],"news_status":{"steam-5335560":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-26T09:32:07Z","status":"ok","all_sources_checked_at":"2026-10-26T09:32:06Z","